From: Nex package maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] path: read system config files from all three UAPI tiers
Source: no upstream commit; written for Nex against mpv dbd7a905
Upstream: not submitted. mpv compiles one system configuration directory, so a
 distribution cannot ship a default that a boot or an administrator may
 override. The change below adds the generic /etc, /run, and <prefix>/lib
 order and names no Nex path, so any Linux system that follows the UAPI
 configuration files specification can use it.

mpv resolved its system configuration directory to a single compiled path,
MPV_CONFDIR, which is /etc/mpv for a normal Linux prefix. mpv.conf, input.conf,
encoding-profiles.conf, and the auto-loaded scripts directory therefore had one
system location each. A package could not ship a default mpv.conf below /usr,
and a boot-time tool had nowhere to put a temporary one.

Split the system location into the three tiers that the UAPI configuration
files specification describes: the lasting administrator directory, then a
temporary directory that one boot owns, then the immutable package directory
below <prefix>/lib. mpv already collects every config file it finds and loads
them lowest priority last-wins, so listing the new directories after "global"
in config_dirs gives administrator over transient over vendor, with the user's
own files still winning over all three. Platforms whose path resolver does not
answer the new types keep exactly one system directory, and --config-dir,
MPV_HOME, and --no-config are unaffected because they still short-circuit
every entry after the first.

diff -urN a/meson.build b/meson.build
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -1750,6 +1750,7 @@
 feature_str = run_command(python, '-c', feature_sort, feature_keys, check: true).stdout()
 conf_data.set_quoted('FULLCONFIG', feature_str)
 conf_data.set_quoted('MPV_CONFDIR', join_paths(get_option('prefix'), get_option('sysconfdir'), 'mpv'))
+conf_data.set_quoted('MPV_VENDOR_CONFDIR', join_paths(get_option('prefix'), get_option('libdir'), 'mpv'))
 conf_data.set_quoted('PLATFORM', host_machine.system())
 configure_file(output : 'config.h', configuration : conf_data)
 message('List of enabled features: ' + feature_str)
diff -urN a/options/path.c b/options/path.c
--- a/options/path.c
+++ b/options/path.c
@@ -62,7 +62,13 @@
     "old_home",
     "osxbundle",
     "exe_dir",
+    // The three system tiers, highest priority first: lasting administrator
+    // policy, then temporary policy that one boot owns, then the immutable
+    // package default. Config files load lowest priority first, so a higher
+    // tier overrides the same option from a lower one.
     "global",
+    "global_transient",
+    "global_vendor",
 };
 
 // Return a platform specific path using a path type as defined in osdep/path.h.
diff -urN a/osdep/path.h b/osdep/path.h
--- a/osdep/path.h
+++ b/osdep/path.h
@@ -8,7 +8,9 @@
 //  "home"          the native mpv-specific user config dir
 //  "old_home"      same as "home", but lesser priority (compatibility)
 //  "osxbundle"     macOS bundle resource path
-//  "global"        the least priority, global config file location
+//  "global"        the lasting administrator config file location
+//  "global_transient" temporary system config that one boot owns
+//  "global_vendor" the least priority, immutable package config location
 //  "desktop"       path to desktop contents
 //
 //  These additional types are also defined. However, they are not necessarily
diff -urN a/osdep/path-unix.c b/osdep/path-unix.c
--- a/osdep/path-unix.c
+++ b/osdep/path-unix.c
@@ -128,6 +128,10 @@
         return mpv_state;
     if (strcmp(type, "global") == 0)
         return MPV_CONFDIR;
+    if (strcmp(type, "global_transient") == 0)
+        return "/run/mpv";
+    if (strcmp(type, "global_vendor") == 0)
+        return MPV_VENDOR_CONFDIR;
     if (strcmp(type, "desktop") == 0)
         return mpv_desktop;
     return NULL;
